# wip660 (E2d of "a project = 2 spots"): a place holds TWO spots: the main one (sounds, patterns 1-16, effects) and a second one (the song, the motion lanes
# and the ARP notes). SAVE writes both, loading a place reads both. A save cut by the power between the two writes loads with no song / lanes / notes (never the
# old ones with the new patterns: the pair mark), and a project too dense for the second spot is refused as MEMORY FULL with NOTHING written (the main spot too).
# (the first empty place is 3 since wip655; place 3 = flash slot 34, place 4 = slot 35: places 1-8 use their override slots 32-39)
wait 300
listen
# --- 1. a project with a hit, two ARP notes, a motion lane (a recorded knob) and a 2-bar song
tapkey b1
key w8 down
tapkey b8
tapkey b9
key w8 up
expect phit0.1.8 1
notepoke 0 0 0 7
notepoke 5 2 4 -3
tapkey w4
tap ENV
key w4 down
spin K1 1
spin K2 10
key w4 up
expect lanes 2
key b10 down
tap SEQ
key b10 up
tap OCT+
tapkey w0
tapkey w1
tap OCT+
expect songlen 2
expect songmode 1
# leave song mode (FUNC + SEQ, OCT+): the song stays, and FUNC + a white key switches patterns again
key b10 down
tap SEQ
key b10 up
expect songask 2
tap OCT+
expect songmode 0
expect songlen 2
expect playing 0
expect slotused34 0
expect extused34 0
# SAVE HERE? (wip708: one screen, the first empty place 3): both spots are written
tap SAVE
expect svhere 3
tap OCT+
expect svstage -1
expect presetcur 3
expect slotused34 1
expect extused34 1
wait 300
# --- 2. another place (4, empty): no notes, no song, no lanes; the place we left is complete when it is loaded again
turn PRESET 1
tap OCT+
wait 300
expect presetcur 4
expect note0.0.0 0
expect note5.2.4 0
expect songlen 0
expect lanes 0
expect phit0.1.8 0
turn PRESET -1
tap OCT+
wait 300
expect presetcur 3
expect phit0.1.8 1
expect note0.0.0 7
expect note5.2.4 -3
expect songlen 2
expect lanes 2
# --- 3. a save cut by the power between the two writes: place 4 gets a changed project (new main spot, new second spot); then its main spot is moved over place 3's
# main spot (presetmove 35 34) = place 3 holds the NEW main spot and its OLD second spot
notepoke 0 0 0 9
tap SAVE
expect svstage 3
turn SELECT 1
expect svhere 4
turn ALGO 1                                   # wip708: a NEW name (SAVE AS made one at every save): the two main spots must differ
tap OCT+
expect svstage -1
expect presetcur 4
expect slotused35 1
expect extused35 1
presetmove 35 34
expect slotused35 0
expect slotused34 1
expect extused34 1
# load place 3: the patterns come (new main spot), the OLD song / lanes / notes do not (their pair mark is the old main spot's)
turn PRESET -1
tap OCT+
wait 300
expect presetcur 3
expect phit0.1.8 1
expect note0.0.0 0
expect note5.2.4 0
expect songlen 0
expect lanes 0
# --- 4. MEMORY FULL: a change in pattern 12 (it would be in the main spot) and 2000 ARP notes (they do not fit the second spot, about 5.8 KB packed)
key b10 down
tapkey w11
key b10 up
expect ppat0 12
tapkey b1
key w8 down
tapkey b8
tapkey b9
key w8 up
expect phit11.1.8 1
notefill 2000
expect dirty 1
tap SAVE
expect svstage 3
tap OCT+
expect svstage -1
said MEMORY FULL
expect dirty 1
expect extused34 1
expect presetcur 3
# nothing was written, the main spot neither: load place 4 (empty), then place 3 again: no pattern 12 hit
turn PRESET 1
tap OCT+
wait 300
expect presetcur 4
turn PRESET -1
tap OCT+
wait 300
expect presetcur 3
expect phit11.1.8 0
# --- 5. the same change with 400 notes (they pack to about 2 KB and fit): saved, and everything is back after another place
key b10 down
tapkey w11
key b10 up
expect ppat0 12
tapkey b1
key w8 down
tapkey b8
tapkey b9
key w8 up
expect phit11.1.8 1
notefill 400
notepoke 0 0 0 7
notepoke 15 7 63 -9
tap SAVE
tap OCT+
expect svstage -1
expect dirty 0
turn PRESET 1
tap OCT+
wait 300
expect presetcur 4
expect note0.0.0 0
expect phit11.1.8 0
turn PRESET -1
tap OCT+
wait 300
expect presetcur 3
expect phit11.1.8 1
expect note0.0.0 7
expect note15.7.63 -9
